    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq",
      "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq",
      "name": "IEEE 1547 grid code compliance testing — frequently asked questions",
      "description": "Common questions about IEEE 1547 and IEEE 1547.1, the equipment a type-test campaign requires, Power-HIL in conformance testing, and in-house pre-compliance.",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#webpage"
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-08-23T09:00:00-04:00",
      "dateModified": "2026-08-23T09:00:00-04:00",
      "author": {
        "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
      },
      "publisher": {
        "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
      },
      "audience": [
        {
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#audience-rts"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#audience-ieee1547"
        }
      ],
      "about": [
        {
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#standard-ieee-1547"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#standard-ieee-1547-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#topic-grid-code-compliance"
        }
      ],
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-1",
          "position": 1,
          "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-1",
          "name": "What is the difference between IEEE 1547 and IEEE 1547.1?",
          "answerCount": 1,
          "inLanguage": "en",
          "author": {
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
          },
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-1-answer",
            "text": "IEEE Std 1547 states the interconnection and interoperability requirements a distributed energy resource must meet — the “what.” IEEE Std 1547.1 specifies the type, production, commissioning, and periodic test procedures used to confirm that equipment conforms to those requirements — the “how.” One defines the obligation; the other defines how it is demonstrated.",
            "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-1",
            "inLanguage": "en",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-2",
          "position": 2,
          "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-2",
          "name": "Is grid code compliance mandatory?",
          "answerCount": 1,
          "inLanguage": "en",
          "author": {
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
          },
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-2-answer",
            "text": "The technical standards themselves are voluntary documents. They become mandatory when a jurisdiction adopts them into its interconnection rules — typically a public utility commission, a network operator, or a regional regulator. In practice, in most developed markets, equipment that cannot evidence conformance cannot obtain permission to operate.",
            "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-2",
            "inLanguage": "en",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-3",
          "position": 3,
          "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-3",
          "name": "What equipment is needed for IEEE 1547.1 type testing?",
          "answerCount": 1,
          "inLanguage": "en",
          "author": {
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
          },
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-3-answer",
            "text": "At minimum: a regenerative alternating-current source capable of independent per-phase voltage, frequency and phase-angle control; a direct-current supply for the equipment input; a measurement path within the required accuracy class; and a sequencer capable of executing and recording the procedures. These can be assembled from separate instruments or delivered from a single cabinet.",
            "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-3",
            "inLanguage": "en",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-4",
          "position": 4,
          "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-4",
          "name": "Can Power Hardware-in-the-Loop be used for conformance testing?",
          "answerCount": 1,
          "inLanguage": "en",
          "author": {
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
          },
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-4-answer",
            "text": "Yes, within the framework the standard sets out. The conformance test procedures standard contains an informative annex addressing hardware-in-the-loop-based testing, including controller hardware-in-the-loop for supplemental devices and Power-HIL setup requirements for unintentional islanding testing. Power-HIL is also widely used for pre-compliance work ahead of a formal campaign.",
            "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-4",
            "inLanguage": "en",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-5",
          "position": 5,
          "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-5",
          "name": "How long does a grid code compliance campaign take?",
          "answerCount": 1,
          "inLanguage": "en",
          "author": {
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
          },
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-5-answer",
            "text": "It varies widely with product readiness and laboratory availability. The type-test programme alone runs to thousands of individual measurement points once every test is repeated across settings, power levels, phase combinations and setting extremes, so manual execution is measured in weeks to months. Automation of the sequence is the single largest lever on that timeline.",
            "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-5",
            "inLanguage": "en",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-6",
          "position": 6,
          "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-6",
          "name": "Why does the same test get repeated so many times?",
          "answerCount": 1,
          "inLanguage": "en",
          "author": {
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
          },
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-6-answer",
            "text": "Because a single pass proves very little. Most procedures repeat across setting extremes, across phases individually and in combination, at multiple power levels, and — for tests where the point on wave matters — at randomised switching instants. The repetition is what converts a favourable result into evidence.",
            "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-6",
            "inLanguage": "en",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-7",
          "position": 7,
          "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-7",
          "name": "What is the non-detection zone in anti-islanding testing?",
          "answerCount": 1,
          "inLanguage": "en",
          "author": {
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
          },
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-7-answer",
            "text": "It is the region in which local load closely matches the resource's own output, so that separating from the network produces almost no change in voltage or frequency. With nothing to detect, an islanding detection algorithm has very little to work with, which is exactly why the test targets that condition deliberately.",
            "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-7",
            "inLanguage": "en",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-8",
          "position": 8,
          "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-8",
          "name": "Do European, UK and Australian grid codes require different test equipment?",
          "answerCount": 1,
          "inLanguage": "en",
          "author": {
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
          },
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-8-answer",
            "text": "Generally no. The functional families are common across modern grid codes — ride-through, grid support, anti-islanding, power quality — so a source that can sag, swell, ramp frequency, step phase angle, unbalance phases and absorb exported power will serve all of them. What differs between regimes is the parameter set, not the hardware capability.",
            "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-8",
            "inLanguage": "en",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-9",
          "position": 9,
          "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-9",
          "name": "Can we do compliance testing in-house, or must it go to an external laboratory?",
          "answerCount": 1,
          "inLanguage": "en",
          "author": {
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
          },
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "@id": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-9-answer",
            "text": "Formal certification is normally issued by an accredited body. In-house testing serves a different and equally important purpose: pre-compliance. Finding a ride-through or settling-time failure on your own bench costs engineering time. Finding it during a booked external campaign costs the campaign.",
            "url": "https://impedyme.com/resource-center/ieee-1547-grid-code-compliance-testing/#faq-9",
            "inLanguage": "en",
            "author": {
              "@id": "https://impedyme.com/#organization"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
